(a) whether it is a fact that 9 million Indians work in the Gulf countries in physically challenging and deadly conditions, facing wage theft and debt crisis;
(b) how many deaths of Indian workers have been reported in Gulf countries during the last five years, year-wise; 
(c) whether the Kafala sponsorship system is still in operation in Gulf countries;
(d) whether any firm steps have been taken to ensure that the rights of Indian migrant workers are not trampled on due to the Kafala system; and 
(e) whether the Ministry would use its influence to improve the working conditions of migrant labourers?

(a) what is the current status of the implementation of Bharat Taxi; 
(b) whether it is a fact that Bharat Taxi implementation across India has not been as successful as initially thought; 
(c) the details of a list of cities where Bharat Taxi has been rolled out, with an average number of daily rides; and
(d) how does Bharat Taxi compare with State Government initiatives in West Bengal?

GK

(a) whether it is a fact that NFSA/PDS is not updated because coverage is based on the 2011 Census, the estimated eligible population vs the covered population now and the number of people excluded from NFSA/PDS;
(b) whether the Ministry would update the coverage despite the Census delay, if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether an interim mechanism would expand coverage to the newly eligible and by when; and
(d) whether the Ministry will consider publishing State-wise coverage-vs-eligible data?

(a) details of the evening-peak deficit and load-shedding, during the summer 2026 heatwave, State-wise;
(b) the manner in which actual firm capacity addition compare to the National Electricity Plan trajectory;
(c) the specific storage/dispatchable-capacity additions that are committed for the next three summers, with timelines; and
(d) whether the department can give the assurance to publish seasonal State-wise peak-deficit and outage data?

(a) the current status of the Broadcasting Bill and does it bring individual digital news creators within its scope;
(b) whether the Bill's provisions on digital creators and content evaluation will be reconsidered;
(c) whether demonetization of social media postings rather than removal will be considered as a preferred route to regulate defamatory/inflamatory/fake news/views flooding social media;
(d) new safeguards to put to prevent the Bill from supressing journalistic and creative expression; and 
(e) whether further public consultation will be held?

(a) the plans to address problems facing the Nirbahya Fund i.e. a long record of under-utilisation of funds and money meant for women's safety too often goes unspent or is slow to reach the ground;
(b) what was allocated, released and actually spent from the Nirbhaya Fund each year, scheme-wise and the real (inflation-adjusted) trend;
(c) reasons of underutilization of funds; and
(d) what steps department propose to take to ensure full, timely utilisation for women's safety?

(a) whether the Indian Customs Electronic Data Interchange System (ICES) is set to be replaced by the new Customs Integrated System (CIS) and the process of vendor selection is ongoing;
(b) whether the Ministry ensures that, unlike the ICES, which was user-friendly only to customs officials but not to transporters, agents and exporters, the new CIS takes into account the convenience of these stakeholders too; and
(c) whether the Ministry ensures that, unlike ICES, which did not encourage digital information exchange with other law enforcement agencies and customs counterparts of other countries, CIS does not suffer from these deficiencies?

(a) the current estimated leakage/diversion of PDS foodgrain, State-wise, and how it is measured;
(b) the reasons for persistence of significant leakage despite digitisation;
(c) whether further measures are planned to cut leakage/diversion;
(d) why storage losses persist and stocks pile up above norms at FCI godowns  while eligible people remain excluded;
(e) whether the Ministry will consider putting Depot-wise loss and Stock data in public domain;
(f) what foodgrain storage and transit losses occurred in the last five years, and the current stock vs buffer norm; and
(g) whether any modernisation and stock-management effort are planned to cut losses?

(a) whether it is a fact that national crude output fell short by over 10 per cent (Apr, 2025 — Jan, 2026) and ONGC cut its FY26 guidance also, ONGC's ~$5-billion KG-DWN-98/2 deep-water flagship badly underperforms, without major new deepwater output, domestic production and self-sufficiency keep falling, pushing import dependence higher;
(b) data-domestic crude/gas production has been vs target for five years, and the KG-DWN-98/2 output vs design and cost; and
(c) any concrete plan to arrest the production decline and improve exploration success?

(a) whether challenges before Government under Jal Jeevan Mission is not coverage but sustained service;
(b) whether it is a fact that only 3/4 of households get regular, safe, adequate water and 83 per cent received water at least once in the previous seven days; 
(c) the share of tap connections that deliver regular, safe, adequate water (as verified), State-wise and the cost per connection vs original estimate;
(d) the proposed steps that will ensure a lasting supply, and by when, State-wise details thereof; and
(e) provide functionality (not just coverage) data State-wise?

(a) whether the commercial model of all social media platforms dictates that the content creators earn money based on engagement (views, likes, etc.) and this model encourages content creators to create content based on shock and awe value rather than facts;
(b) whether the Ministry will consider framing a policy to demonetize the clips/reels of news/views channels working under the guise of freedom of expression but spewing venom and defamatory content; and
(c) whether the Ministry will consider framing the policy so that freedom of expression is protected on these social media platforms, but the right to earn money through that expression cannot be claimed?

(a) whether NCAP is set to miss its 2026 target and Delhi's average PM10 exceeded its NCAP-baseline level during 2024-25;
(b) whether against ?11,211 crore released under NCAP/XV-FC (2019–25), only ~68% (?7,594 cr) was utilised;
(c) whether the Ministry also failed to ensure the installation of manual stations for monitoring against the target; and
(d) the city-wise NCAP targets vs achievement funds released vs utilised; and 
(e) the steps to meet clean-air goals with a revised timeline?

(a) the current status of the implementation of Bharat Taxi;
(b)  whether it is a fact that implementation of Bharat Taxi across the country is suffering because of administrative ineptitude; and
(c) how does Bharat Taxi compare with the State Government initiatives in West Bengal?

(a) whether Section 43B(h) of the Income Tax Act disallows a tax deduction to buyers until they actually pay a micro/small supplier, to enforce the 45-day timeline;
(b) whether the enforcement of this section has led to large and medium buyers cancelling orders with registered MSMEs;
(c) whether the buyers are forced to shift to unregistered vendors, or pressurize small suppliers to surrender their Udyam registration; and
(d) whether the section affects only the Udyam-registered suppliers, the steps the Ministry has taken to rectify the challenges, if any?

(a) whether there is any plan to make the UPI related data without customer private details available in the public domain (with some govt fees) so that new business models can come up;
(b) whether ?210 cr annually is spent on maintaining technological operations and ?290 crore as depreciation on the cost, a one-paise charge per UPI transaction to merchant will cover the technological operation cost, as number of transactions are approx 17 billion per year, and 2 paisa would cover almost all the cost and make UPI, financially self-sustainable; and 
(c) whether the Ministry is considering making UPI operations self sustainable?
